# udev rule for the RTK base F9P on the Raspberry Pi.
#
# Creates the stable symlink /dev/f9p_base pointing at whatever ttyACM* the
# u-blox ZED-F9P enumerates as. Mirrors the pattern used on the NUC for the
# rover's helical F9P (/dev/f9p_helical).
#
# u-blox ZED-F9P USB IDs:
#   idVendor=1546 (u-blox AG)
#   idProduct=01a9 (u-blox GNSS receiver)
#
# If you ever plug a SECOND u-blox receiver into the Pi (e.g. a rover during
# bench testing), both will match this rule. In that case, add a serial-number
# match too: ATTRS{serial}=="..." — find it with `udevadm info -a -n /dev/ttyACM0`.

SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1546", ATTRS{idProduct}=="01a9", SYMLINK+="f9p_base", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"
